From: "Claude (SGR dev session)" <claude@sgr-dev.local>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 03:53:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test(exchanges): cover PionexAdapter (26% -> 100%)

- Add tests/exchanges/test_pionex.py: 15 tests covering
  sgr/exchanges/pionex.py's PionexAdapter, the primary Pionex
  exchange integration used across the trading lifecycle
  (Order Management -> Pionex Execution). Note: the existing
  tests/exchanges/test_pionex_client.py tests a different module
  (pionex_client.py, the raw REST client), not this adapter.
- Reuses the FakeCCXTExchange/install_fake_ccxt monkeypatching
  pattern already established in tests/exchanges/test_ccxt_base.py
  to exercise real adapter code paths without network access.
- Covers: __init__ (exchange_id/_ccxt_id/_testnet_urls={}, extra
  options merge for adjustForTimeDifference), connect() Paper Mode
  (happy path loading public market data only, ccxt-not-installed
  RuntimeError, load_markets failure with cleanup, close()-failure-
  during-cleanup still re-raises the original error), connect() Live
  Mode (delegates to CCXTBaseAdapter.connect()), from_config()
  (paper mode with configured dummy credentials, paper mode fallback
  placeholder credentials, live mode with real credentials, live
  mode raises ValueError when credentials missing).
- No production code changes. Full suite verified green: 1041
  passed, 9 skipped, 0 failed. Coverage 87.29% -> 87.85%. ruff
  unchanged (22, pre-existing). mypy unchanged in sgr/ (118,
  pre-existing); new test file's untyped-def mypy findings follow
  the same established convention already present in
  test_ccxt_base.py (105 similar findings there), not a new
  regression - tracked mypy baseline is sgr/ only.
